    "body": "# PR type\r\n- [x] Bug Fix\r\n- [ ] New Feature\r\n- [ ] Document Updates\r\n- [ ] More Models or Datasets Support\r\n\r\n# PR information\r\n1、HCCL permission verification\r\nAdd HMAC authentication. This signature verification occurs before `pickle.loads()`; without the secret key, an attacker cannot forge a valid signature, ensuring that malicious pickle payloads are never deserialized.\r\n(1) Upon startup, the main process generates a 256-bit random key and distributes it to authorized workers via `HCCLMasterMetadata`.\r\n(2) `_send_pyobj`: Instead of using `send_pyobj()`, the data is first serialized via `pickle.dumps()`. An HMAC-SHA256 signature is then calculated, and the combined data—consisting of the 32-byte signature followed by the payload—is sent.\r\n(3) `_recv_pyobj`: Instead of using `recv_pyobj()`, the system uses `recv()` to retrieve the raw bytes. It extracts the first 32 bytes (the signature) and verifies them using `hmac.compare_digest`. Only if the verification succeeds is `pickle.loads(payload)` called; otherwise, the data is rejected.\r\n\r\n## Experiment results\r\n\r\nPaste your experiment result here(if needed).\r\n\r\n# Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] I have linked the related issue above, if there is one.\r\n- [ ] I have reviewed and understand every changed line, and I can explain how the change works and why it is correct.\r\n- [ ] I have run the relevant tests or reproductions locally, and included the commands and results above (if applicable).\r\n- [ ] I am responsible for the content of this PR, regardless of how it was produced.\r\n",
